WHERE THE STATUS COMES FROM -- SETTLED
--------------------------------------

A line drawn across the activity curve that doc 008 already defines. Above the
line the actor is closed; below it, open. Busy is closed. Rest is open.

Nothing new is authored and nothing new is drawn. The 225 by 30 widget already in
the tome becomes the instrument that shows a rigid life at a glance, and the
impact ratio is readable straight off the shape -- a curve with two narrow troughs
is a person whose two open hours land with enormous force.

    hours   0  3  6  9 12 15 18 21
    curve   _  .  #  #  #  -  .  _
            ------------------------  the line
    status  O  O  |  |  |  O  O  O

    and the life the city insists on:

    curve   #  #  #  #  #  #  #  #
    status  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |
            never open. nothing reaches her.

This retroactively explains a sentence doc 008 wrote without knowing what it
meant: "a curve pinned high all day is telling you something about that person."
It is telling you they are never open.

And it gives "you must work a job" a mechanism instead of a mood. The rigid life
is a curve shape, and the city enforces it by filling the day.
